@@ -0,0 +1,119 @@
+---
+name: fix-selection
+description: "Generate distinct fixes for one frozen symptom, execute their oracles/regressions/metrics, and require evidence-bound role-panel selection before applying production changes."
+type: skill
+---
+
+# Evidence-bound fix alternatives
+
+Generate at least two distinct source proposals from the diagnosed cause, not
+merely two explanations of the same diff. Compare only under the same frozen
+acceptance/oracles. A plausible first patch or a declared cost is insufficient.
+
+## Workflow
+
+1. Analyzer prepares fresh primary/independent oracle files and acceptance/normal
+   cases in the ticket workspace's `oracle-kit/`, preserving existing tests.
+   Use the ticket symptom, not a conveniently different failure. A faithful RED
+   proof is still required by the analysis transition; missing reproduction is
+   BLOCKED. The source baseline remains the immutable intake/RED source.
+2. Planner proposes 2..8 materially distinct fixes and freezes the evaluation
+   axes/directions/units/required flags/tolerances, regression and metric adapters,
+   three role judges and their adapter source SHA256 before executing the trials.
+   Declare the actual root-cause edge, scope, rationale and tradeoffs per proposal.
+3. In DESIGN, run `scripts/fix_selection.py`. It carries only new test/oracle/
+   requirement artifacts into a RED commit using a separate Git index; no source
+   checkout/index/default branch is changed. Existing baseline files cannot be
+   rewritten to manufacture RED. It materializes trial commits, uses WI-V1 at
+   each explicit candidate ref, and executes frozen regression/metric adapters.
+4. The panel receives source diffs, hard results, measured axes, and role-specific
+   evidence hashes. Correctness cites the oracle result, regression cites the
+   executed regression receipt, maintainability cites source. Each member records
+   an accept/reject/abstain reason and a preference or null. Judge origin is
+   explicit (`model`, `human`, `fixture`); an origin label is not independent
+   human approval. Do not pass private history/settings/logs as review evidence.
+5. Only a hard-eligible, unanimously accepted and preferred unique measured
+   Pareto candidate is SELECTED. Missing required measurement, abstention,
+   conflicting judgments/preferences, no comparable axes, or tradeoff/tie returns
+   DEFERRED/TIED; all rejected returns REJECTED. There is no weighted sum or
+   automatic first-candidate fallback. Revise evidence/criteria explicitly in
+   planning, never after-the-fact to make a favored patch appear better.
+6. Bind spec/report byte hashes and selected commit in `states.DESIGN`. Before
+   DESIGN→IMPLEMENTATION run `--check`. Implementer uses the prepared RED carrier
+   and applies the selected source tree on its isolated fix branch, preserving
+   the intake base. Do not create a second RED carrier or silently alter the fix.
+7. Before EVALUATION/COMPLETION run `--check --applied`; altered source trees need
+   re-evaluation. Run WI-V1 again at actual current HEAD. Candidate-trial oracle
+   receipts cannot substitute for final current-HEAD evidence. Other build/race/
+   lint/security/chain/regression gates remain mandatory.
+
+## fix-selection-spec.json
+
+Version1 contains:
+
+- `source_base_ref`: full unfixed commit SHA, `oracle_plan`: workspace-relative
+  WI-V1 template path. Its base_ref must equal source_base_ref.
+- Optional `oracle_sources`: subject frozen path → workspace source path for
+  **new** carrier files. Allowed new files are under oracles/tests, `_test.go`,
+  or the declared requirements/derivation. Existing baseline files stay identical.
+- `criteria`: `selection_rule: unanimous-panel-and-pareto`, `axes`: 1..8 objects
+  `{id,unit,direction:min|max,required:boolean,tolerance:nonnegative number}`.
+  `changed_lines` is measured by Git; other IDs require executed metric adapters.
+  Document each role's minimum, target workload and comparison limits.
+- `regression_driver`, `metric_drivers` (at most8): `{command:[argv...],source_file}`;
+  the adapter source must be in the frozen oracle files. Regression emits JSON
+  `{schema_version:1,candidate_id,subject_commit,status:PASS|FAIL|ERROR}` and exits0
+  when it successfully reports the observation (FAIL is not transport failure).
+  Metric adapters emit the same identity plus `metrics:{id:{value:number|null,unit}}`.
+  Nonfinite/duplicate/wrong-source/error data cannot authorize selection.
+- `judges`: three distinct IDs and roles correctness/regression/maintainability,
+  each with `kind`, `command`, absolute local `adapter_source`, `adapter_sha256`.
+  For a Claude model, use `scripts/claude_fix_judge.py`; it starts a fresh tool-free
+  CLI review with settings sources/MCP/session persistence disabled. The provider
+  still uses its configured authentication. No credentials belong in the packet.
+- `candidates`: 2..8 `{id,rationale,commit_subject,changes,mutants}`. Commit subject
+  is short English `fix: ...`. `changes` has 1..12 distinct text files and exact
+  `{path,before,after}` replacements. `before:null` adds a new file; `after:null`
+  deletes only when before is the exact full baseline file. Frozen files cannot
+  be changed. Source mutants are specific replacements for each alternative,
+  while all other acceptance/oracle parameters remain common.
+- `timeout_seconds` (per adapter, default120, max300), `max_total_seconds`
+  (default1800, max7200). Oversized artifacts/outputs or incomplete execution is
+  not PASS. Judge IDs/roles/candidate coverage and citations are validated.
+
+The report stores commits/trees/diffs and their hashes, actual WI-V1 runs and
+raw adapter/model outputs, measured versus judged values, rejected/deferred
+reasons, source/adapter identities, and the selected tree. It states the result
+only for observed proposals/axes, not the globally best possible fix. Independent
+human acceptance remains `not_recorded` unless separately reviewed.
+
+## Commands and guards
+
+```bash
+python3 "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/fix_selection.py" --workspace "{workspace_dir}" --repo "{repo_root}"
+python3 "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/fix_selection.py" --workspace "{workspace_dir}" --repo "{repo_root}" --check
+python3 "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/fix_selection.py" --workspace "{workspace_dir}" --repo "{repo_root}" --check --applied
+```
+
+Record SHA256 of spec/report and `selected_candidate_commit` under states.DESIGN.
+Copy the selected candidate's `oracle_plan_bytes` into oracle-validity-plan.json,
+set states.ANALYSIS.oracle_validity_plan_sha256 and
+states.IMPLEMENTATION.reproduction_commit to report.oracle_base_commit. These
+are the same carrier/oracles used by trial execution; changing them invalidates
+selection. At actual HEAD generate a fresh V1 report and bind its SHA normally.
+
+The Write/Edit `fix-selection-guard.py` enforces selection at implementation
+entry and exact selected tree at evaluation/completion, and freezes criteria
+identity. Direct shell/manual writes are outside the hook; Orchestrator must
+run both read-only selection and oracle CLI checks before any PR side effect.
+Neither gate grants permission to push/merge.
+
+## Verification
+
+`test_fix_selection.py` exercises real source proposals, trial oracles/regression,
+tamper/stale/missing/disagreement/tie/unknown cases. `selection_smoke.py --panel
+fixture` labels fixture opinions explicitly; `--panel model` executes actual
+configured Claude reviewers and retains their raw receipts. It uses an owned Go
+repository with two valid fixes and a literal overfit, measured allocation count,
+and final current-HEAD/guard checks. No production or independent-human quality
+claim follows from this controlled example.
